# dsk_tradeui: the TRADE SCREEN of Teropoly (deskopoly M9) driven through the REAL deskopoly_driver, in a scratch house, ONLY by deskopoly_ctl command lines (what each button of the popup and of the four panes runs).
# What the screen publishes is the feed state/game_ui.txt (tp_on, tpa/tpg/tpr/tpb panes, the popup text and buttons, game-ov_y); what the game KNOWS is the ledger: every check below reads one of the two.
# THE GAME: tests/../fixtures/dsk_tradeui_ledger.txt = 47 rows of an engine-made 3-player game (seed 7; A = human p1, B and C pets), cut where p1 is to act in PRE of round 5 with 930 cash and tiles 12 Power, 19 Orange3,
#   26 Yellow1; p2 owns 21 Red1 and 27 Yellow2 (960 cash); p3 owns 8, 15, 24, 31, 35 (530 cash). It is the engine's own output (rebuilt with lobby/join/start/order/tick/roll/buy/end_turn), replayed by the driver at start, never edited.
#   p1's first roll (ctl `roll`) lands on 33 and KEEPS a Get Out (fund) card, which the card checks use. The switch running stays 0 for the whole case, so no pet ever acts: every ledger row below is the human's or a CLI call that says who.
# RULES COVERED: panes (titles, item order, counts, the paging of a long inventory), moving a tile in and out, cash +-10 and its clamps, partner cycling clears GET, Send builds `offer`; MODES: new / counter (swapped terms, partner fixed,
#   stays open when it is not my turn) / amend (my terms, partner fixed) / cancel; a carried-over card can be taken back out; the screen closes itself (turn passes; the offer under a counter vanishes).
# A pet-made offer to the human cannot be produced by the pets yet (pet proposals are another agent's work): the offers addressed to p1 are made by the engine CLI `offer p1 ... as=p2` while p2 is the current player, the same verb a pet will use.
# NEGATIVES (each is paired with a positive control that proves the same keys CAN change): a tile p1 does not own, a tile the partner does not own, cash above what is held and below zero, Send with an empty draft, a partner change in counter/amend,
#   draft commands with the screen closed, hostile ctl strings, an out-of-range tile number; the screen closing itself.
# FENCE: a command that must change NOTHING is followed by one that visibly changes something; the driver handles action lines in order and publishes once per pass, so seeing the fence proves the earlier line was handled.
# NOT COVERED: the real window's drawing (tests/dsk-seat-counter.pdl looks at the PNGs), pets answering offers (dsk_trade covers the engine side), the CPU cost.
RESULTS | ../results/dsk_tradeui.txt
ENV | LC_ALL | C

CASE    | setup
SCRATCH |
MKDIR   | h/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x
COPY    | &.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/raw_to_png.+x | h/&.widgits/_shared-lib/ops/+x/raw_to_png.+x
COPYDIR | @.apps/deskopoly | app | state,shots
# 2026-11-09: the screens show the DECK DISPLAY NAME from page.pdl (LABEL chest), not the engine word `fund`; pinned here so a rename of the real label does not break this case
APPEND  | app/rulesets/classic/page.pdl | LABEL \p chest \p Lost & Found\n
MKDIR   | app/deskopoly-pchq/pieces/system/maps/deskopoly/play
MKDIR   | edit/state/world
MKDIR   | edit/edit-pchq/pieces/world_01
MKDIR   | edit/state/games/deskopoly/game
WRITE   | edit/state/world/switches.txt | running=0\n
WRITE   | edit/edit-pchq/pieces/world_01/state.txt | map_id=deskopoly\ndesk_id=board\n
COPY    | &.widgits/_shared-lib/harness/fixtures/dsk_tradeui_ledger.txt | edit/state/games/deskopoly/game/ledger.txt
RUN | $T/app/ops/+x/deskopoly.+x | $T/app | $T/edit/state/games/deskopoly/game | replay
EXPECT_OUT | REPLAY events=47 | the-fixture-is-a-valid-engine-ledger-47-rows
SPAWN   | OWN | /usr/bin/sleep | 600
ENV     | GAME_OWNER_PID | $OWN
SPAWN   | DRV | $T/app/ops/+x/deskopoly_driver.+x | $T/h | $T/app | $T/edit
WAIT_HAS | edit/state/game_ui.txt | a game was in progress | 8000 | the-driver-continues-the-game-from-the-ledger
EXPECT_HAS | $T/edit/state/game_ui.txt | \nphase=pre\n | p1-is-to-act-in-PRE
EXPECT_HAS | $T/edit/state/game_ui.txt | \nhuman_turn=1\n | and-it-is-a-human-turn
EXPECT_HAS | $T/edit/state/game_ui.txt | \ntp_on=\n | NO-TRADE-SCREEN-before-it-is-opened
EXPECT_LACKS | $T/edit/state/game_ui.txt | tpa_title | and-no-pane-keys-at-all
RUN | $T/app/ops/+x/deskopoly_ctl.+x | roll | $T/edit/state/games/deskopoly
WAIT_HAS | edit/state/games/deskopoly/game/ledger.txt | to=33;card=fund:5;keep=fund | 8000 | p1-rolls-to-33-and-keeps-a-Get-Out-fund-card
WAIT_HAS | edit/state/game_ui.txt | gmb_1_label=Trade... | 8000 | the-Trade-button-is-in-the-popup-after-the-roll-POST-phase
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -c | ^ | $T/edit/state/games/deskopoly/game/ledger.txt
EXPECT_OUT_IS | 48 | 47-plus-the-roll

CASE    | panes
